TensorFold patch 0004: tuning of patch 0002's prompt expert kernel (prefill_kernel).

- K stages of 64 (2 deep) instead of 32 (3 deep): half the block barriers a pass, which were ~1.9 stall cycles an
  issued instruction (Nsight Compute, 2026-10-12).
- The prefill kernel's mma without ``volatile`` (a pure function of its registers), each K tile's B fragments of
  both column tiles decoded before its multiplies: the compiler may interleave decode and mma ("wait" stalls were
  ~3 cycles an issued instruction).
- The second launch (a width other than 4 bits) is sized for what the layer holds: up to 6 bits (Flash Next's
  shared expert) with the same stages; wider, K stages of 32 so its shared memory fits.
- Extension renamed tensorfold_exl3_experts_v3.
Results are unchanged (each output's K sum is in the same order; tests/cuda/test_exl3_prompt_experts.py). A Flash
Next layer's experts at 4096 rows: 17.3 -> ~16.8 ms.

Base: TensorFold 609ca419 + the recipe's vision-prefix-cache.patch + local 0001-0003.

